## How slow was the response

!! The first warning reached one phone at 03:58 and was not acknowledged. Escalation to the backup took until 04:35, and the backup acknowledged at 04:52, 54 minutes after the first warning. The freezer had been above its -18 C limit since 04:05, and it took 90 minutes from the compressor fault to the manual reset.

data stages = Stage,Start,End; Fault to first warning (03:40 to 03:58),0,18; Warning to escalation (03:58 to 04:35),18,55; Escalation to backup ack (04:35 to 04:52),55,72; Ack to compressor reset (04:52 to 05:10),72,90; Reset to back below -18 C (05:10 to 07:30),90,230

chart range stages from=Start to=End unit=min target="25 above -18 C at 04:05" title="Minutes after the 03:40 compressor fault"

## What we know and what we do not

### Known

- Freezer 3 air was above -18.0 C from 04:05 to 07:30, 3 hours 25 minutes.
- The highest air reading in the log was -11.2 C at 05:10.
- Compressor B faulted with E-41 (low suction pressure) at 03:40 and the system switched to Compressor A, which tripped on overload at 03:41.
- The BMS did not log the Compressor A trip until 03:58, 17 minutes later.
- The on-call phone did not acknowledge. He says it was on charge in another room.
- Compressor B was last serviced 14 months ago against a 12-month schedule.
- A third alarm channel (SMS to the shift supervisor) was proposed in April and was not done.
- 18 pallets (3-14 to 3-31) were tagged for quarantine at 07:45.
- A core probe at 09:00 read -17.1 C.
- Cost so far is $9,850.

### Not known

- The peak core temperature of any pallet. It was not measured.
- The peak air temperature between readings. The log holds readings at event times only, so -11.2 C is the highest logged value, not necessarily the true peak. The sensor's continuous record should be checked.
- Why Compressor B had low suction pressure, and why Compressor A tripped on overload.
- Why the BMS took 17 minutes to log the Compressor A trip.
- Where the 04:05 above-limit alarm was sent, and to whom. The log does not show it reaching anyone.
- Whether anyone from the night shift was on site at 03:58. The loading dock was in use at 02:14.
- The exact time the backup contact reached the site. The log records the acknowledgement and arrival in one entry at 04:52, with a 17-minute drive.
- Whether the 02:14 door alarm played any part. Temperature was back to -20.1 C by 03:40, and we have no evidence it contributed.
- The condition of the other two clients' stock. The log records no assessment of it.

## Root causes

cards

### Equipment

Compressor B faulted and Compressor A tripped within a minute, so there was no working compressor. The service on B was 2 months overdue. Overdue service is a contributing factor; we have not shown it caused the fault.

### Alerting

One warning, to one phone, with no one else told. Nothing reached anyone on site. The shift supervisor SMS channel that would have been a second route was proposed in April and never built.

### Escalation

After the unanswered warning the escalation to the backup took until 04:35, and the backup then had a 17-minute drive. Nobody was alerted that the freezer had crossed its limit at 04:05 other than by the same route.

## Corrective actions

All owners and dates below are proposed and need to be confirmed.

data actions = No.,Action,Addresses,Owner (proposed),Due (proposed); 1,"Send the distributor the full record and ask for their decision on pallets 3-14 to 3-31; keep the quarantine until then",Impact,QA (Mei-Lin Zhao),2026-10-23; 2,"Add the SMS alarm to the shift supervisor (the third channel proposed in April)",Alerting,Operations director,2026-10-30; 3,"Send warnings to on-call and backup together; if not acknowledged within 10 minutes, escalate automatically to the shift supervisor",Escalation,Operations director,2026-11-06; 4,"Find out why Compressor B showed E-41 and why Compressor A tripped on overload; service Compressor B",Equipment,Facilities,2026-10-30; 5,"Check every compressor's service date against its schedule and book the overdue ones",Equipment,Facilities,2026-11-13; 6,"Find out why the BMS logged the Compressor A trip 17 minutes late",Alerting,Facilities with the BMS supplier,2026-11-13; 7,"Write a procedure to take product core readings at the alarm and every 30 minutes until the freezer is back in range",Evidence,QA,2026-11-20; 8,"Run an after-hours drill of the whole alarm chain once the new channels are live, then each quarter",Escalation,Operations director,2026-11-27

table actions

## Cost

The estimated cost so far is $9,850 for the call-out, repairs and extra QA time. It does not include any loss of product, which depends on the distributor's decision.
